Wizard: Fix validation errors not clearing upon user selection

Persona: Non-technical business owner (e.g. Maya the baker).
Browser/Playwright flow attempted: Starting on `setup.html`, proceed to the "Set up your Assistant" step. Click "Next" without selecting a team or a tone to trigger validation errors. Then, select a team and a tone.
CUJ gap observed: After making a selection, the validation error message and the red border around the input remained visible, confusing the user into thinking their selection was invalid.
UX reason for fix: Immediate feedback is crucial for form validation. Users should not have to click "Next" again just to see if their action fixed the error.
Post-fix flow: Following the same steps, selecting a team now immediately clears the "Please select an AI agent team." error and the red border. Similarly, selecting a tone immediately clears the "Please select a tone." error and its red border. E2E tests have been added to verify this behavior, and the test suite has been repaired from a broken state caused by earlier debugging.

Loaded superpowers: none.
